    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d601">

                <pb facs="0641" n="629" sameAs="frus:frus1945v08/pg629"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">881.00/8–1145: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Spain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Armour</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">San Sebastian</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-08-11T00:00:00+02:00">August 11,
                            1945—midnight</date>.<lb/>[Received August 12—12:10 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>SS12. British Ambassador<anchor n="55" xml:id="d601-f1"/> and French
                    representative have received notes from Foreign Office here informing them that
                    Spanish <pb facs="0642" n="630" xml:id="pg630"/> Govt not having been invited to
                    participate in preliminary Tangier discussions at Paris wishes it to be
                    understood that it reserves all its rights as a signatory of the 1923
                    statute.</p>
                <p>Repeated Paris, London, Tangier and by courier to Madrid.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Armour</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d601-f1" n="55" xml:id="d601-f1-content">
